        "notes": "The private self-name is initialized to the created function once during the original call, before parameter defaults, and is retained by the suspended frame and nested closures rather than overwritten by a later resumption's callee. Existing assignment semantics ignore writes in non-strict code and throw TypeError in strict code. Eval-dependent variants remain unsupported."
      },
